z5b = z1z + ledger (bots/zl0) + THROW_ADAPT (u7i's doctrine, ledgered; Cfg.THROW_ADAPT; Baby.throwSeen, sawThrower,
retreat). Once a baby has seen an enemy rat carrying one of ours, it never retreats to our king again (RETREAT_HP 40
otherwise sends a baby at 40 hp or less near enemies home). Hooks: after the sense loop (K 18) and at the head of
retreat() (K 20 with its if).

Evidence (build/dumpcache, 105 replica matches, 315 games; scratch kthrown.py, kgrab.py, kgrab2.py, kdis.py): all 567
enemy thrown-rat hits on our kings threw one of our rats (20,609 damage), 300 point-blank (42 to the king, 42 to the
rat). Of 604 traced grabs, the victim stood Chebyshev 3-5 from the hit king's centre in 454. None had the grabber in
its 90-degree cone, though chance would put about 37% there. 458 victims were weaker than the grabber, and in 57% the
grabber had been in the victim's cone a turn earlier: wounded rats walking home turn their backs on it. Carriers within
Chebyshev 4 of our kings made 80% of the king damage (18,605), 90% of it by thewaxmango (8,717) and nzjt (7,996). u7i
(THROW_ADAPT on u6x) pooled D 14, net +8, t +2.14 over two replica blocks. It was rejected on its registered Merlin
falsifier (throw hits 5.3 a game, bar < 4). u9r (on u9p, unledgered) failed the old absolute picks bar at zd63.

Falsifiers, registered before any z5b game:
1. Screen zd184 (vs zd136) on the s6 gates: t <= -1.5, picks/100 per-cell z <= -2, ppr per-round z <= -2, transfer
   per round < 0.97x, any overrun.
2. Replica (bundled onto the incumbent line after z3x is decided): the block rules plus the transfer floor against
   the twin. Mechanism: in the candidate's block games against thewaxmango and nzjt, enemy hits on our kings with
   our thrown rats (kthrown.py, deduplicated) must be at most half the twin's per game in the same blocks. u7i's
   failure mode must not recur: a cell against YokoOno or Varun that the twin won and the candidate lost counts
   against it, and two such cells drop it.
